Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: enable the S905X2 VIU encoder routing driver

The G12A tree lacks the vout_mux device used by vout_func_update_viu.
Without a bound mux driver that helper silently returns, leaving the VIU
on the bootloader encoder. A boot with the HDMI receiver off can start
in CVBS (ENCI); subsequent progressive HDMI uses ENCP but receives no
VPP vsync, so DRM page flips time out and the screen remains black.

Add the same generic mux device used by G12B/SM1 to the tested S905X2
board. The existing kernel driver then selects the encoder from vinfo,
including interlaced modes, instead of relying on the bootloader route.
No register constants or timing overrides are needed.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/g12a_s905x2_u212_2g_rtl8822cs.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/g12a_s905x2_u212_2g_rtl8822cs.dts
@@ -5,6 +5,11 @@
     model = "S905X2 u212-compatible 2GB RTL8822CS";
     amlogic-dt-id = "g12a_s905x2_u212_2g_rtl8822cs";
     coreelec-dt-id = "g12a_s905x2_u212_2g_rtl8822cs";
+
+    vout_mux {
+        compatible = "amlogic, vout_mux";
+        status = "okay";
+    };
 };
 &{/vpu} { clk_level = <8>; };
 &{/reserved-memory/linux,meson-fb} {
